# Docker
dev.Dockerfile
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore

# Git files
#
# `.gitignore` is deliberately NOT here. Tailwind's automatic source
# detection honours it, and the build writes `.nuxt/` and `.output/`
# while it runs. Without `.gitignore` the client and SSR environments
# (`experimental.viteEnvironmentApi`) scanned different generated files,
# emitted two different `entry.*.css` files, and the page loaded both:
# the chunk-linked one landed later in `@layer utilities`, so its base
# utilities beat the other's `lg:` ones (v3.205.1's hero stayed at its
# phone ratio on desktop). tailwindlabs/tailwindcss#19888; the local
# build, which has `.gitignore`, emits exactly one.
.git

# Env files — never bake local/real secrets into the build stage
.env
.env.*

